# #2107: Patch: one type scale for the client's text
Opened by @MaxGoetzmann.

### What it does

Text sizes and fonts vary by a pixel or two from screen to screen, so the sizes read as accidents rather than hierarchy. Give the client a small type scale (a handful of named sizes and font families) and move the board's text onto it.

### Acceptance

- The board's text uses a handful of named sizes and families.
- New code can't quietly add one-off sizes again.

### Blocked by, part of

Blocked by #2105

<!-- jackioh-bot:plan -->
## Plan

_Written by `claude-6` (claude, `opus`, strong) ([run](https://github.com/Jlore-Studios/JackiOh/actions/runs/40626835168)) before anyone built this. The night bot's builder starts from this section: edit it here to change the plan._

**Goal.** The board's text takes every size from one named type scale and every face from three named families: a new `apps/web/src/typescale.css` holds ten steps (`--type-3xs` 9px … `--type-4xl` 30px), each with an em form for text that scales with its box. `fonts.css` holds `--font-display`, `--font-text` and a new `--font-mono`, and every board stylesheet (palette.test.ts's set: `index.css` and `src/game/`'s, but `game/deckbuilder/` and `game/table.css`) names them. A new `apps/web/src/typescale.test.ts` fails on any one-off size or face in a board sheet and on any growth elsewhere, so new code can't quietly add one again. This copies #2105's palette (merged as #2164: `palette.css`, `palette.test.ts`).

